<h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
<div class="prose">
  <p>I make sound interactive, and sometimes musical. My work explores new ways to interact with
  sound by building digital musical instruments and musical robots — installations where the line
  between audience and performer stops mattering, and anyone who walks up can play.</p>

  <p>I came to this sideways: electrical engineering at CU Boulder, seven years designing chips at
  Xilinx, then a master's in Music, Science and Technology at Stanford's CCRMA, and a PhD at CU's
  ATLAS Institute on scaffolded design tools for interactive music. The engineering never went
  away; it just started serving the music.</p>

  <h2>Teaching</h2>
  <p>I teach and develop courses at the ATLAS Institute (CU Boulder) and Inworks (CU Denver) —
  Creative Technology, Physical Computing, Internet of Things, Digital Fabrication, Human Centered
  Design — plus workshops for makers from about age eight through adult. Hands-on, learn-by-doing,
  share and critique.</p>

  <h2>B.E.A.T.</h2>
  <p>In 2019 I founded <strong>Boulder Experiments in Art and Technology</strong>, a community for
  people working at the intersection of art, technology, and science. We meet, share what we are
  building, and occasionally put on a show.</p>

